<title>USA: Third Ave Funds takes Tejon Ranch stake.</title>
<headline>Third Ave Funds takes Tejon Ranch stake.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Third Avenue Funds, a $1.3 billion open-end mutual fund group, said Thursday it had acquired about 26 percent of the outstanding common stock of Tejon Ranch Co, which owns land in California.</p>
<p>Tejon is also involved in commercial real estate, farming, ranching, recreation, filming and mineral extraction.</p>
<p>The fund said Third Avenue Value Fund acquired 3.05 million Tejon shares, and Third Avenue Small-Cap Value Fund acquired 200,000 shares from Times Mirror Co, which previously announced its intention to divest itself of investments that did not relate to its core businesses.</p>
<p>((--New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
